{"h":3209,"w":2400,"lines":[{"x":0.66601942137116132,"y":0.039244186130346304,"c":1,"t":"Sample Writing answers","w":0.22912620544433593,"h":0.015988371899566145},{"h":0.021929109282211257,"c":1,"w":0.35728154500325521,"x":0.06019417888265053,"t":"TEST 4, WRITING TASK 1","y":0.088662790550699588},{"w":0.80593566894531254,"t":"This model has been prepared by an examiner as an example of a very good answer.","h":0.019598616840683425,"y":0.12670362405680835,"c":1,"x":0.060130535084989369},{"t":"From the line graph, we can see the average monthly rise or fall in how much copper, nickel and","h":0.02448661423917875,"c":1,"w":0.80800435384114577,"x":0.060092390384733581,"y":0.15431606545965637},{"y":0.17855791642289121,"w":0.22759440104166667,"h":0.022177908353716358,"c":1,"t":"Zinc cost throughout 2014.","x":0.058031840642841295},{"w":0.80794820149739577,"c":1,"t":"Overall, nickel started with the highest percentage change of the three but ended with the lowest.","h":0.025330217307973135,"x":0.060094754001174235,"y":0.20498605945494608},{"x":0.060123207127622987,"w":0.79430984497070301,"c":1,"y":0.22813996482488785,"t":"Zinc started with the smallest change and ended with the highest, and copper prices fluctuated.","h":0.022213609641957621},{"w":0.35728154500325521,"h":0.019003115264797588,"c":1,"y":0.25140186901364436,"x":0.060194178864841019,"t":"Prices for all three metals dipped in June."},{"h":0.022227088238962689,"w":0.80204900105794263,"t":"In January the price of nickel was up six per cent, but this dropped to negative three percent in","c":1,"y":0.27899258381296255,"x":0.058202591856906072},{"t":"June, ending the year with a one percent increase in both November and December. Copper began","c":1,"w":0.82535664876302084,"x":0.060139753736604004,"y":0.30054823267491892,"h":0.022348817486629313},{"y":0.32244028137327663,"h":0.021903169340805051,"c":1,"x":0.060145465193855427,"w":0.81369903564453128,"t":"the year with an increase of two percent and by May, the price was dropping (by slightly less than"},{"h":0.024875700288101044,"t":"one per cent). It rose again, increasing by a percentage point in July, August and September. Zinc","x":0.060086845809440209,"y":0.34245952480463271,"w":0.81963572184244793,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.36546039001860664,"t":"saw its most dramatic increase in February, with three per cent and the price fell in June (a one","x":0.060119697094707381,"w":0.80598490397135403,"h":0.022366987804757432},{"t":"percent decrease). The change was negative until October\/November when it began to rise.","y":0.38808139481414095,"h":0.020348838259497959,"c":1,"x":0.062135934491688166,"w":0.75922327677408852},{"c":1,"y":0.4258566980616475,"h":0.016003766758048266,"t":"Here are comments from another examiner:","x":0.064077678352074424,"w":0.41359222412109364},{"x":0.10868467001458536,"y":0.46242613152185119,"h":0.019232989397375722,"c":1,"w":0.72245803833007816,"t":"This response reports the main data for each of the three metals. There is an"},{"x":0.10485436341945027,"w":0.76116505940755208,"c":1,"t":"introduction in the first paragraph and an overview in the second, followed by the","h":0.017445482866043527,"y":0.48255451724181997},{"c":1,"x":0.10865436974156371,"t":"presentation of the main trends of all three categories in the third. Some details are","y":0.4995291466141103,"w":0.77879175821940105,"h":0.019749893949039254},{"w":0.75546880086263024,"c":1,"h":0.019744446418738515,"x":0.10867305273831733,"y":0.51841091856532651,"t":"missing (copper after September and no percentage changes for any metal from"},{"h":0.017453633364858612,"y":0.53924418592627477,"w":0.18834952036539715,"c":1,"t":"July to September).","x":0.10873786107620111},{"y":0.57412790724871721,"c":1,"w":0.77864079793294261,"h":0.019018510123279597,"x":0.10873785340246069,"t":"The candidate identifies the 'dip' for all three in June, but to score more highly, they"},{"x":0.1086836619049716,"c":1,"t":"could also have mentioned that overall, percentage changes fell at the beginning of","y":0.59275157776368481,"w":0.78265935262044262,"h":0.021480771834233803},{"y":0.61067815899436806,"x":0.10670551219302828,"t":"the year, remained static from July to September and rose after October to the end","w":0.7788520812988281,"h":0.020552146174826036,"c":1},{"t":"of the year.","c":1,"x":0.10823272947662119,"w":0.10993723551432291,"h":0.018698912766120901,"y":0.63103991326485653},{"y":0.66647484901019205,"c":1,"w":0.75932922363281252,"x":0.10674388751804524,"h":0.020527489682967137,"t":"Information is arranged coherently; each metal is taken in turn for data reporting."},{"t":"There is good use of cohesive devices [Overall | but | with | when], but there could","h":0.020369939120759017,"c":1,"y":0.68482646667720637,"w":0.76906794230143227,"x":0.1086781901463714},{"h":0.013755049660941099,"t":"be more.","c":1,"x":0.10848622589266796,"y":0.70821964353553346,"w":0.089825013478597004},{"c":1,"t":"Vocabulary is adequate with some attempts to use less common items [fluctuated |","w":0.77875544230143223,"x":0.10868559872739231,"y":0.74101438203332293,"h":0.018720431936864235},{"c":1,"x":0.11067961847431661,"t":"dramatic increase] and attempts to use synonyms [ended with the lowest | dipped |","h":0.017491668629869173,"y":0.76012461054802272,"w":0.77669901529947916},{"w":0.091521046956380206,"h":0.01683362800384236,"t":"droppedj.","x":0.11055015603006212,"y":0.78155411621150772,"c":1},{"w":0.77873972574869788,"h":0.020252101815006807,"t":"There is a lack of complex structures, as most sentences are simple or compound.","c":1,"x":0.10868609359491047,"y":0.8163824932322673},{"w":0.73220530192057287,"c":1,"t":"However, there is some variety in structures, including comparatives [highest |","y":0.8346792091198536,"x":0.11060748329722989,"h":0.020281360899547907},{"w":0.60597381591796873,"t":"smallest | most dramatic] and continuous tenses [was dropping].","x":0.10865091115614746,"y":0.85302961955134082,"h":0.019996550372827882,"c":1},{"w